</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 307)</h2>
<p><b>Clients can request originals — you stay in charge.</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Original-file delivery, end to end: a web reviewer requests a clip's original, you approve (or pre-approve per share), and the file uploads encrypted in chunks and downloads straight to their disk, decrypted in the browser. Byte-exact, end-to-end encrypted, wiped with the review.</li>
<li>Off by default, and only you can turn it on — "Allow original-file requests" in the Share to Web sheet. Requests arriving while it's off are refused by the app itself, and the web tells clients that enabling is the host's call. Passphrase-protected shares always require manual approval.</li>
<li>Every delivery writes a session note, so the report records who received what.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
